.TH "SKOGAI RUNNER-WO-NEW" 1  "skogai runner-wo-new 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai runner\-wo\-new \- scaffold a workorder
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai runner wo new\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME>
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-schema\fR=\fISCHEMA\fR
.br
output schema, default answer
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR=[\fIFILE\fR]...
.br
input files
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tools\fR=\fITOOLS\fR
.br
tools the worker may use
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-allow\fR=[\fIALLOW\fR]...
.br
allowed tool patterns, e.g. "Bash(git log *)"
.TP
\fB\-\-sandbox\fR
.br
the worker runs in a sandbox, see wo run
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
.br
kebab\-case name
